{"title":"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/5/9353c907a64b80423cb6b7575208cbf994ae0429.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(1,0)--(1,4)--(0,4)--(0,0)--(0,1)--(-1,1)--(-1,2)); draw((-1,2)--(0,2)--(0,4)--(-1,4)--(-1,5)--(1,5)--(1,6)--(0,6)); draw((0,6)--(0,5)--(3,5)--(3,6)--(4,6)--(4,2)--(5,2)); draw((5,2)--(5,1)--(1,1)--(3,1)--(3,0)--(4,0)--(4,1)); draw((1,4)--(3,4)--(3,2)--(1,2)--(4,2)--(3,2)--(3,6)); draw((3,6)--(4,6)--(4,5)--(5,5)--(5,4)--(4,4)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Four rectangular paper strips of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and width <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are put flat on a table and overlap perpendicularly as shown. How much area of the table is covered?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afe3db068b59204b405b36d010b9465578254473.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 36 \\qquad  \\text{(B)}\\ 40 \\qquad  \\text{(C)}\\ 44 \\qquad  \\text{(D)}\\ 98 \\qquad  \\text{(E)}\\ 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"387\" height=\"18\" />    \n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first notice that the paper strips cover up part of the others. Since the width of the overlap is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the length of the overlap is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the area of \neach of the strips with the overlap is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/b/45bda479bb39886ca64a1bfce93d4c07a30ddf38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10\\cdot 1)-1=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />. Since there are 4 strips, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/0/8d07746a7fb1898cc46b42aa05a543829d373655.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\cdot 9=36 \\implies \\boxed{\\text{A}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME\" title=\"1988 AHSME\">1988 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1988 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1988\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1988 AHSME Prob